#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166482 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "113b981d-bbf2-588a-be74-028506cdb19d" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching the Phase Portrait of a System"}] :question/id #uuid "8337af7a-73e8-5ae2-9bed-b03f193b2950" :question/math-academy-id "e-21657" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear differential equations below.\n${x^{′}(t) =-y(t); y^{′}(t) = 9x(t)$\nThe eigenvalues of the system's matrix are $\\lambda_{1,2} = \\pm3\\text{i}$, for which the corresponding eigenvectors are $\\mathbf{v}_{1,2} = [\\pm \\text{i}, 3]^T$, respectively. Given that the general solution of the system is\n$\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}$\nsketch the phase portrait of the system of differential equations given above." :question/worked-solution "We are given that the general solution of the system is\n$\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nFor example, when $c_1=1$ and $c_2=0$, we obtain the following curve:\n\n$$\n{x =-\\sin (3t); y = 3\\cos (3t)\n$$\n\nComputing the coordinates (rounded to two decimal places) of several points on the curve, we get the table below.\n\n| $t$ | $0$ | $\\dfrac{\\pi}{12}$ | $\\dfrac{\\pi}{6}$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $x$ | $0$ | $-0.71$ | $-1$ |\n| $y$ | $3$ | $2.12$ | $0$ |\n\nLet's sketch this solution in the phase space.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3241/Source/Images/53de9c32f79277beb9f683133f7b0cf5.png)\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n\\mid \\sin(3t) \\mid \\leq 1\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\mid \\cos(3t) \\mid \\leq 1\n$$\n\nThus, the obtained curve is bounded. So, we have an ellipse that is traversed counterclockwise.\n\nThe phase portrait of our system looks as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3241/Source/Images/3d7278b105e7e6f65eb433ca671c6a4e.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166483 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b542bd66-f4f8-5b4e-a3e7-4717827c427a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Parameters of a System Given Its Phase Portrait"}] :question/id #uuid "7b4f569b-ad3a-5a93-a53e-27a186b7700e" :question/math-academy-id "e-21658" :question/problem "The phase portrait for a system of linear differential equations whose matrix has two complex eigenvalues $\\lambda = a \\pm b\\text{i}$ is shown above. Provide an interpretation of the portrait and determine the possible values of $a$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3241/Source/Images/6b0386ae3c66a70a85c39b440c659e81.png)" :question/worked-solution "Let\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{v}=\\mathbf{p}+\\mathbf{q}\\text{i}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf{p},\\mathbf{q} \\in \\mathbb{R}^2$, be an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue\n\n$$\n\\lambda = a + b\\text{i}\n$$\n\nThen, a complex solution of the system is given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}_{\\text{complex}}(t) = \\mathbf{v} e^{\\lambda t}\n$$\n\nUsing Euler's formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx_{complex}(t) &= ve^{(a + b\\textrm{i})t} \\\\\n&= e^{at}(\\cos (bt) + \\textrm{i}\\sin (bt))(p + q\\textrm{i}) \\\\\n&= e^{at}(\\cos (bt)p - \\sin (bt)q) + \\textrm{i}e^{at}(\\sin (bt)p + \\cos (bt)q)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\textbf{x}(t) = c_1 e^{at}\\big(\\cos(bt)\\mathbf{p}-\\sin(bt)\\mathbf{q}\\big) + c_2 e^{at}\\big(\\sin(bt)\\mathbf{p}+\\cos(bt)\\mathbf{q}\\big)\n$$\n\nwhere the parts $\\big(\\cos(bt)\\mathbf{p}-\\sin(bt)\\mathbf{q}\\big)$ and $\\big(\\sin(bt)\\mathbf{p}+\\cos(bt)\\mathbf{q}\\big)$ are bounded.\n\nNow notice that the given curve is unbounded, representing a spiral that is traversed counterclockwise. Thus, we must have\n\n$$\na \\neq 0\n$$\n\nAlso, notice that the spiral is traversed toward the origin.\n\nHence, to insure that $e^{at} \\to 0$, we require $a < 0$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166484 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f0b176c-c802-5b3b-85d0-dede602c9bf3" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying Systems of Linear Differential Equations With Complex Eigenvalues"}] :question/id #uuid "d7b40689-7b7e-546e-9b66-30e6a95f3ee0" :question/math-academy-id "e-21659" :question/problem "${x^{′}(t) =-2y(t); y^{′}(t) = 2x(t)$\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are $\\lambda=\\pm2\\text{i}$. Provide an interpretation of the equilibrium point (origin) for the system of differential equations given above." :question/worked-solution "Let\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{v}=\\mathbf{p}+\\mathbf{q}\\text{i}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf{p},\\mathbf{q} \\in \\mathbb{R}^2$, be an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue\n\n$$\n\\lambda = a + b\\text{i}\n$$\n\nThen, a complex solution of the system is given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}_{\\text{complex}}(t) = \\mathbf{v} e^{\\lambda t}\n$$\n\nUsing Euler's formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx_{complex}(t) &= ve^{(a + b\\textrm{i})t} \\\\\n&= e^{at}(\\cos (bt) + \\textrm{i}\\sin (bt))(p + q\\textrm{i}) \\\\\n&= e^{at}(\\cos (bt)p - \\sin (bt)q) + \\textrm{i}e^{at}(\\sin (bt)p + \\cos (bt)q)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\textbf{x}(t) = c_1 e^{at}\\big(\\cos(bt)\\mathbf{p}-\\sin(bt)\\mathbf{q}\\big) + c_2 e^{at}\\big(\\sin(bt)\\mathbf{p}+\\cos(bt)\\mathbf{q}\\big)\n$$\n\nwhere the parts $\\big(\\cos(bt)\\mathbf{p}-\\sin(bt)\\mathbf{q}\\big)$ and $\\big(\\sin(bt)\\mathbf{p}+\\cos(bt)\\mathbf{q}\\big)$ are bounded.\n\nNow, notice that\n\n$$\na = \\text{Re}(\\lambda) = 0\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\ne^{at} = e^{0\\cdot t} = 1\n$$\n\nfor all $t$. Thus, we have an ellipse that curves around the origin.\n\nTherefore, since\n\n$$\n\\text{Re}(\\lambda) = 0\n$$\n\nthe equilibrium point (origin) is a center."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167180 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b542bd66-f4f8-5b4e-a3e7-4717827c427a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Parameters of a System Given Its Phase Portrait"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bbdb4242-e289-599d-b91c-c1c65288b6c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "an ellipse" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164487} {:answer/id #uuid "1e66c076-3feb-5cda-9118-e6d6aa331b59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a spiral" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164488}] :answer-field/id #uuid "e60614b8-2386-5a59-9612-5ab470b0735b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164486} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ce1bbceb-ffd5-5324-80b6-d51d2ffde118" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "bounded" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164490} {:answer/id #uuid "2687fe5f-cd9c-5397-82c9-2c85b1282082" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "unbounded" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164491}] :answer-field/id #uuid "f09c7f01-9a00-5ee4-9361-aa84f7bd9ab9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164489} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d14d5ba3-c9c1-5ca7-b9c8-feea13268525" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "counterclockwise" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164493} {:answer/id #uuid "e08ccc1c-cb15-58e5-b5be-7c51067fb4d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "clockwise" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164494}] :answer-field/id #uuid "7cac7fc7-dd8c-5a3b-b7ea-f54cdf056f6e" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164492} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "105ef604-50ac-5d85-b608-120d61a6f12e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164496} {:answer/id #uuid "7468be2d-b74c-58c6-aa6b-07d0d0cba6fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a ≠ 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164497} {:answer/id #uuid "7dc6397e-9c81-51b5-a7ac-f4d8b97504cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164498}] :answer-field/id #uuid "8c077598-41ce-5ab6-9b35-341bce326be0" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164495}] :question/id #uuid "84ee34e5-631b-5bc6-a73e-d75bd75ac74d" :question/math-academy-id "q-334290" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3241/Source/Images/q-334290.png)\n\nThe phase portrait for a system of linear differential equations whose matrix has two complex eigenvalues $λ = a ± b\\textrm{i}$ is shown above. Select the correct options in the reasoning below.The given curve is\n{{field-1}},\nrepresenting\n{{field-2}}\nthat is traversed\n{{field-3}}.\nThus, we must have\n{{field-4}}."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167181 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f0b176c-c802-5b3b-85d0-dede602c9bf3" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying Systems of Linear Differential Equations With Complex Eigenvalues"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9eb863cc-b64c-59da-990d-72c5097ec568" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Re(λ) = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164500} {:answer/id #uuid "dd925b62-7df9-59ae-8801-d43cdadfbc3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Im(λ) > 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164501} {:answer/id #uuid "f5d9d43b-79f9-5bce-8a81-9ee0b3052dc2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Im(λ) < 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164502} {:answer/id #uuid "26fa26b1-d002-5f14-865a-c49d65fd08b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Im(λ) = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164503} {:answer/id #uuid "44f1a013-c9fe-55ef-b9fc-e94548b27bda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Re(λ) < 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164504} {:answer/id #uuid "5c83c56d-4c38-5958-96df-2e6f16b3ee76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Re(λ) > 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164505}] :answer-field/id #uuid "506935cf-0014-5880-ba52-9296f3404e2d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164499} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f2924cbd-1802-555c-a71c-4c97991ae569" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a stable spiral (sink)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164507} {:answer/id #uuid "fc31666a-a649-5555-b52f-6c546d19728e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a center" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164508} {:answer/id #uuid "7aa8e2f8-8cf8-5664-820a-75a38d782cf7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "an unstable spiral (source)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164509}] :answer-field/id #uuid "b2d6e791-1b7b-5ae3-8e93-1ae5f5ff6d08" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164506}] :question/id #uuid "dd7f6a8a-46ea-55af-8487-3a48b0b2a59e" :question/math-academy-id "q-334307" :question/problem "${x^{′}(t) =-2x(t) - 5y(t); y^{′}(t) = 5x(t) - 2y(t)$\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are $λ =-2 ± 5\\textrm{i}$. Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\nSince\n{{field-1}},\nthe equilibrium point (origin) is {{field-2}}."}]}
